    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's what I did to unify the two identifiers into a single `memberId`.\n\n## Summary\n\n**New format** \u2014 `memberId` = `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`: region code, 2-digit fiscal year of the registration date, the 8 upper-hex SHA-256-over-(normalizedTelephone+lastName) HASH8 (the same one the old region-and-hash identity used), and a single Luhn check digit over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`. The AUDIT line confirms it: `memberId=NSW2616E6609E3` (NSW \u00b7 26 \u00b7 16E6609E \u00b7 3).\n\n**Where the logic lives**\n- **`util/MemberId.java`** (new, replaces `CustomerCode`) \u2014 builds the id, de-duplicates collisions by appending `-<n>`, and reads the REGION and FY segments back out (fixed-width tail parsing, dedup-suffix aware). CHK reuses `util/Luhn`; HASH8 reuses `util/Sha256`.\n- **`function/owner/AssignMemberId.java`** (new, replaces `AssignCustomerCode` + `AssignMembershipNumber`) \u2014 one step assigns the id, so collision handling now applies to `memberId`.\n- **`util/FiscalYear`** \u2014 added a `label(String)` overload so the `FY` prefix convention isn't duplicated where the fiscal year is rebuilt from the id's segment.\n\n**Threaded through everywhere the old fields flowed**\n- `model/Owner` \u2014 `customer_code`/`membership_number` fields \u2192 single `member_id`; `getPrimaryIdentifier()` returns it.\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper` \u2014 dropped the standalone `checkDigit` field; `locality` (\u2192 owner segment) and `fiscalYear` now both read their segments back out of `memberId`, so it's the single source of both derivations.\n- `AuditOwnerCreated` + `OwnerCreatedEvent` \u2014 audit line and structured event now carry `memberId`.\n- `openapi.yml` (DTO codegen), the four dialect `schema.sql` files, and the `owners.POST.yml` wiring/comments \u2014 old fields removed, `memberId` added.\n\nDoc references in `OwnerRegion`, `Sha256`, `FiscalYear`, and `ApplyRegistrationDate` were updated to point at the new identity. The one existing test plus the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 run / 0 failures).\n\nOne design decision worth flagging: the spec's phrase *\"the fiscal-year value \u2026 must reference the memberId\"* \u2014 I read the FY back out of `memberId` in the mapper (mirroring how `locality` reads REGION out of it), making the id the single source of truth. The alternative reading is to keep deriving `fiscalYear` from the registration date directly; both yield the same value, but I chose the former to satisfy the sentence literally and keep the design symmetric. Easy to switch if you intended the other.",
